      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The resort community was founded in 1902, featuring an inn, a recreational complex, and a cottage village.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pocono_Manor_Historic_District",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Pocono Manor Inn grew in nine sections from 1902 to 1949, with the first seven designed by Walter Smedley.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18,
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pocono_Manor_Historic_District",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Quakers originally developed the cottage community, which showcases Stick/Eastlake, Shingle Style, and Bungalow/American Craftsman designs.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pocono_Manor_Historic_District"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The district contains 75 contributing buildings, one site, four structures, and four objects across the historic resort grounds.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pocono_Manor_Historic_District"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Pocono Manor sits in Monroe County, bounded roughly by PA 314, Lake and Cliff Roads, and Summit Avenue.",
